  "paper_text": {
    "limitations_or_appendix": "Post-hoc power analysis (80\\% power, $\\alpha=0.05$, two-sided) yields minimum detectable effect sizes (MDES) of 1.2--2.0\\,pp for MMLU ($n_{\\text{treated}}=3{,}540$, $n_{\\text{untreated}}=10{,}502$) and 2.3--5.6\\,pp for ARC-Challenge ($n_{\\text{treated}}=257$, $n_{\\text{untreated}}=915$). All observed $|\\text{DiD}|$ values fall below the MDES (MMLU: 0.3--1.1\\,pp; ARC: 0.2--2.4\\,pp), meaning the test cannot distinguish a true null from a sub-2\\,pp effect on MMLU. However, this bound rules out the large item-specific effects ($>$5\\,pp) that characterize memorization-based contamination in prior work."
  }
